  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the joystick of each human fighter, from fighter two_players down to fighter 0. Not in the demo."},
    {"at":13,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the joystick of fighter X and selects the next move. Fighter 0 uses port 2 ($dc00), fighter 1 port 1 ($dc01)."},
    {"at":23,"placement":"side","text":"No input during the walk-in, the time-out, the set-up, the turn, or after a kill."},
    {"at":25,"placement":"side","text":"Moves $1b, $08 and $13 ignore the joystick."},
    {"at":43,"placement":"side","text":"Direction table for the facing of the fighter."},
    {"at":53,"placement":"side","text":"Bits 0-4 of the port: 1 = pressed."},
    {"at":70,"placement":"line","text":"Stores the input A in fighter_input. Returns Y = 0-8: none, forward, back, down, up, down-forward, up-forward, down-back, up-back. Y = $ff for no match."},
    {"at":84,"placement":"line","text":"Sets move_ptr to the row of 9 next moves for the current move. Uses table $ce1e with fire, $ce02 without fire. Keeps Y."},
    {"at":111,"placement":"side","text":"move_ptr = $ce3a + 9 x row."},
    {"at":126,"placement":"line","text":"Starts the move of row entry Y unless the current move is locked or is the same. Sets the first pose."},
    {"at":130,"placement":"side","text":"Idle move $1a: stays while there is no direction."},
    {"at":156,"placement":"side","text":"Bit 7 of the table entry locks the new move."},
    {"at":160,"placement":"side","text":"Move script: table $bc87."}
  ],
